um: release NT mm context in arch_exit_mmap when mm_users reaches 0

On standard Linux, exit_mmap() frees all user pages when mm_users drops
to 0 (__mmput), before MMF_OOM_SKIP is set and before lazy-TLB or
oom_mm mm_count references are dropped. On UML-NT, guest physical runs
live in mm->context.id.nt_conn and were only freed in destroy_context()
(__mmdrop when mm_count hits 0), stranding 15-25 MiB of physical runs
per exiting or OOM-killed process until PID 1 reaped the zombie.

Hook arch_exit_mmap(mm) to call destroy_context(mm) under
CONFIG_OS_WINDOWS so guest physical runs are released immediately in
exit_mmap(). Since uml_nt_mmctx_destroy zeroes id->nt_conn, the later
destroy_context(mm) in __mmdrop is a no-op.

Signed-off-by: uml-nt agent <droid@factory.ai>
---
 a/arch/um/include/asm/mmu_context.h | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/um/include/asm/mmu_context.h
+++ b/arch/um/include/asm/mmu_context.h
@@ -24,6 +24,10 @@
 #define destroy_context destroy_context
 extern void destroy_context(struct mm_struct *mm);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_OS_WINDOWS
+#define arch_exit_mmap(mm) destroy_context(mm)
+#endif
+
 #include <asm-generic/mmu_context.h>
 
 #endif
